# Testing: Module Test

Purpose:
   Specify module test requirements including regression testing
   for ensuring previous module functionality remains intact.

Owns: testing/module-test.sdd

ModuleTest:
   purpose: Verify entire module functionality and prevent regressions
   scope: All subtasks within a module combined
   owner: QA agent + implementer agent
   trigger: When all STs for a module are DONE
   execution: local Docker (test-runner service)
   frequency: Per module completion

Requirements:
   [MODULE1] Must test all STs in the module as an integrated unit
   [MODULE2] Must include regression tests for previous module functionality
   [MODULE3] Must run in Docker container ([R102])
   [MODULE4] Must produce JUnit/XML test reports
   [MODULE5] Must generate coverage reports when applicable
   [MODULE6] Must fail if any ST in the module has regressions
   [MODULE7] Must pass before SYSTEM level testing can begin

TestTypes:
   - Integration (T1): Verify STs work together
   - Component (T3): Verify complete module in isolation
   - E2E (T4): Verify user journeys within module scope
   - Note: Unit tests (T0) run at SUBTASK level, not MODULE level

RegressionTesting:
   purpose: Ensure new changes don't break existing functionality
   scope: Previously working module features
   owner: QA agent
   trigger: Module test execution
   execution: local Docker (test-runner service)
   
   Requirements:
     [REG1] Must test previously implemented STs
     [REG2] Must compare against baseline behavior
     [REG3] Must fail if regressions detected
     [REG4] Must be automated and repeatable

Navigation:
   TestHierarchy: @../workflow/test-hierarchy.sdd
   LocalTestExecution: @../workflow/local-test-execution.sdd
   DockerCompose: @../../docker-compose.yml
   TestRunner: @../codding/Dockerfile.test-runner
   MicroUnit: @../workflow/micro-unit.sdd

State: +
   (Module test specification with regression requirements)
   (Owner: QA + implementer)
   (Execution: local Docker)
   (Regression testing included)